    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Initialization Scripts for Agents Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements `init_agent.py`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Five probes: Python version, listed dependencies via `importlib.util.find_spec`, test command resolvability, required env vars, state file freshness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Each probe returns `(name, status, detail)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- The script writes `init_report.json` with the full probe set and exits non-zero if any block-severity probe fails."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The script prints the table of probes, writes `init_report.json`, and exits zero on the happy path or non-zero with a list of failed probes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a probe that diffs the current commit against the last-known-good commit and refuses to start if more than 50 files changed.\n2. Wire the script to write a `prereqs.lock` file and refuse to start if the lock is older than seven days.\n3. Add a `--fix` flag that auto-installs missing dev dependencies but never modifies runtime dependencies without approval.\n4. Move probes from hardcoded functions to a YAML registry. Defend the trade-off.\n5. Add a timing budget per probe. A probe that runs longer than three seconds is a workbench smell."
      ]
    }
  ],
